(vector (map (:db/id -1), (:adr/id "2607242400"), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-* -- ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor, round 3: extend from 21 to 31 of ~155 repos, built via parallel subagents"), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/date "2026-07-24"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242000-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242300-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round2.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn")), (:adr/scope-still-not-fleet-wide "this ADR extends the actor layer to 10 MORE cloud-itonami-lei-* repos (31 of ~155 total after this round). ~124 repos remain untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. Owner asked to continue the same batch-of-10 pace, this time built via parallel Agent-tool subagents (one per company) instead of serial main-loop construction, for wall-clock efficiency"), (:adr/batch-companies "cloud-itonami-lei-1b4s6s7g0tw5ee83bo58 (American Electric Power Company Inc, US-OH), cloud-itonami-lei-254900ug5d8yst164n14 (Xero Limited, New Zealand -- first NZ-jurisdiction company in this actor family), cloud-itonami-lei-52990083zrr5ut591988 (Nexstar Media Group Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-529900vbk42y5hhrmd23 (BlackRock Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300dejzcpwa4hkm93 (FirstGroup plc, GB), cloud-itonami-lei-549300j0dyc0n31v7g13 (Workday Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300vsgcj7e698nm85 (The Charles Schwab Corporation, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-8eu0xufvj48u37iidh51 (Casella Waste Systems Inc, US-VT), cloud-itonami-lei-c4bxaty60wc6xeozdx54 (MetLife Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-ni14y5umu60o7je9p611 (Adecco Group AG, Switzerland -- first CH-jurisdiction company) -- again an evenly-spread sample of the remaining pool (134 repos after round 2), not cherry-picked"), (:adr/parallel-subagent-construction "each of the 10 repos was built by an independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent, given a single self-contained prompt specifying: the exact template files to copy verbatim from the pilot repo, the exact per-company customization scope (tosmonitor.store demo data + README + docs/adr/0001 only), the real blueprint.edn/tos.journal.edn metadata for that company (read and supplied by the orchestrating session, not re-derived by the subagent), the required lint/test bar (0 errors, 25/70 tests passing) before commit, and the exact git workflow (sync main, branch, commit, push, PR via gh with explicit --head/--base, merge --merge --delete-branch, return to main). No two subagents touched the same repository, so no cross-agent coordination or isolation mechanism was needed beyond assigning disjoint company directories"), (:adr/identical-code-per-company "tosmonitor.governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor remain byte-identical across all 31 repos now carrying this actor. Only tosmonitor.store's company/baseline demo data, README.md, and docs/adr/0001 differ per repo, same convention as rounds 1-2"), (:adr/test-status-batch10-round3 "each of the 10 repos independently passes its own governor contract (6 HARD checks + high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants, store parity (MemStore/DatomicStore), and advisor smoke tests -- verified by each subagent before commit, spot-checked by the orchestrating session after merge"), (:adr/local-loop-established "as part of this round, a self-paced continuation loop (ScheduleWakeup-based, via the workspace's `loop` skill) was set up so future batches of 10 can continue without the owner re-issuing the request each time; see the loop's own configuration/first wakeup record for its exact re-entry prompt and pacing"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607242400: cloud-itonami-lei-* ToSMonitor round-3 batch-of-10, subagent-built\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607241900 (pilot); ADR-2607242000 (round 1, found/fixed two real\n  bugs); ADR-2607242300 (round 2, validated the corrected template against three\n  new jurisdiction/doc-type firsts with zero further code changes needed);\n  ADR-2607110300 (archive-only design still governing the other ~124 repos).\n\n## Context\n\nWith 21 of ~155 repos carrying a real, tested governed actor across two prior\nrounds and zero outstanding template defects, the owner asked to continue\nexpanding, this time explicitly asking for two efficiency/durability changes:\n(1) build each company's repo via a parallel Agent-tool subagent instead of\nserial construction in the main session loop, and (2) set up a local/self-paced\ncontinuation loop so future rounds do not require the owner to re-request each\ntime -- mirroring the `/loop`-based continuation pattern ADR-2607199960 already\nestablished for this same `cloud-itonami-lei-*` catalog's discovery/onboarding\nwork.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **10 more repos** (31 of ~155 total), again evenly sampled from the\n   remaining pool. Two new jurisdiction firsts: Xero Limited (New Zealand) and\n   Adecco Group AG (Switzerland).\n2. **Parallel subagent construction.** Each company was assigned to one\n   independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent carrying a fully self-contained\n   prompt (template file paths, real archive metadata pre-read by the\n   orchestrating session, the exact lint/test bar, and the exact git\n   workflow) -- no subagent needed to rediscover the pattern from scratch, and\n   no two subagents touched the same repository, so parallel dispatch required\n   no additional coordination or isolation mechanism.\n3. **Same bar, no relaxation.** Each repo still independently passes its own\n   governor-contract/phase/store-parity/advisor tests and gets its own PR+merge.\n4. **A self-paced continuation loop was established** (via this workspace's\n   `loop` skill) so subsequent batches of 10 can proceed without the owner\n   re-issuing the request each session, consistent with ADR-2607199960's own\n   precedent for long-running `/loop`-based work on this same catalog family.\n5. **Still not fleet-wide.** ~124 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos remain untouched,\n   governed solely by ADR-2607110300.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Wall-clock time for a 10-repo round drops substantially versus serial\n  construction, since each company's build+test+PR+merge is fully independent\n  of every other company's.\n- (+) The self-paced loop removes the per-round manual re-request friction,\n  matching how ADR-2607199960 already handles this catalog's other long-running\n  discovery work.\n- (+) Validated the pattern against two more jurisdiction firsts (NZ, CH) with\n  the byte-identical template, reinforcing round 2's finding that the\n  round-1 fixes were the real remaining gaps.\n- (-) Parallel subagent construction means the orchestrating session verifies\n  each subagent's work post-hoc (spot-checking merged output) rather than\n  watching every step live, a real (if so far unrealized) risk of a subagent\n  silently deviating from the prompt that serial construction did not carry.\n- (-) An unattended self-paced loop still requires periodic owner attention to\n  confirm it should keep going -- it does not remove the standing question of\n  whether/when to stop before reaching fleet-wide coverage.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607241900, ADR-2607242000, ADR-2607242300, ADR-2607110300, ADR-2607199960\n  (the `/loop` continuation precedent for this catalog family)\n- The 10 repos' own `docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` records\n")))
